<title>UK: Barclays says raises UK base rate to 6.25 percent.</title>
<headline>Barclays says raises UK base rate to 6.25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Barclays Bank Plc said on Tuesday it had increased its base rate by 25 basis points to 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>The move, which takes effect today, followed on the heels of the decision by the new Labour government to push up rates from 6.0 percent to 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
